{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261017T014648Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "c9a6184923cc1a5837b49001", "title": "Welcome Beam: a 501B open model you can own, customize, and scale", "url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/reflection-beam", "source": "Hugging Face - Blog", "published": "2026-10-16T00:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.9425, "worthiness_confidence": 0.81, "final_score": 0.9425, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 26777, "delivered": true, "summary": "Reflection released Beam, a 501B-parameter sparse MoE model with 23B active parameters per token, designed for coding and agentic tasks with 1M token context. The model features hybrid attention (sliding-window plus global layers), expert parallelism routing, and ships with native support in transformers, vLLM, and SGLang. For builders, Beam matters because it's fully open-source, customizable via LoRA or full-parameter fine-tuning with provided TRL and Miles recipes, and runs efficiently on existing hardware through multiple quantization formats (BF16, FP8, NVFP4). The key takeaway: deploy on 4 B200s or 8 H200s with speculative decoding for production inference, or fine-tune with LoRA on a single 8-GPU node for domain adaptation.", "jev_ms": 173.1, "jev_input_tokens": 8079, "jev_cost": 0.000339318, "llm_ms": 3877.1, "llm_cost": 0.009196, "errors": []}
