{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261017T014648Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "58d2e800a62db5e14019818a", "title": "Hyper Optimizing Kimi K3 in vLLM: Moving Fast and Responsibly", "url": "https://vllm.ai/blog/2026-10-16-kimi-k3-megakernel", "source": "vLLM Blog", "published": "2026-10-16T00:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.9575, "worthiness_confidence": 0.86, "final_score": 0.9575, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 13742, "delivered": true, "summary": "vLLM optimized Kimi K3 decode performance on NVIDIA GB300 GPUs using agent-assisted kernel development with CuTe DSL, achieving 842 tokens/s at batch 1 on 16 GPUs and 1.5–2× throughput gains across configurations. The work matters because AI engineers need production-ready inference optimizations that balance performance with reliability. The key takeaway: adopt systematic validation practices—isolate changes to model code, bound scope to specific hardware/workloads, validate correctness with both kernel tests and long-context evaluations, and measure performance across batch sizes—to enable fast agent-driven optimization without sacrificing code quality.", "jev_ms": 161.6, "jev_input_tokens": 3633, "jev_cost": 0.000152586, "llm_ms": 3162.3, "llm_cost": 0.004205, "errors": []}
{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261017T014648Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "83c8b3ad5c31c776c9d699ef", "title": "Scaling Kimi K3 on AMD Instinct MI355X: Matching NVIDIA HGX B300 Throughput per GPU on AgentX", "url": "https://vllm.ai/blog/2026-10-16-kimi-k3-mi355x", "source": "vLLM Blog", "published": "2026-10-16T00:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.98, "worthiness_confidence": 0.93, "final_score": 0.98, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 24523, "delivered": true, "summary": "vLLM achieved 24.4% higher throughput per GPU serving Kimi K3 on AMD Instinct MI355X versus NVIDIA HGX B300, translating to 87.4% more tokens per dollar. Key optimizations include decode context parallelism reducing MLA cache from 1.96GB to 245MB per GPU, fusing KDA recurrent operations into single kernels, eliminating duplicate MoE expert projections via all-reduce, and padding MLA heads to enable AMD AITER assembly for 1.85× faster long-context attention. The takeaway: systematic profiling of data movement, kernel handoffs, and parallelism across model architecture layers reveals substantial efficiency gains without algorithmic changes.", "jev_ms": 173.6, "jev_input_tokens": 6538, "jev_cost": 0.000274596, "llm_ms": 3629.9, "llm_cost": 0.007505, "errors": []}
